## Problem

# `b00t learn <topic>` loads a skill/pattern but the commands it teaches are always
# available, regardless of whether training was acknowledged. This creates two risks:
# 1. Agent invokes a blessed command WITHOUT having read the failure modes or syntax.
# 2. Pattern/idiom/jargon datums have no first-class type — they float as `Unknown`.

# Concretely: the fdfind guard redirects from `find`, but nothing verifies the agent
# actually knows `fdfind` syntax before the redirect. A blessed command needs a
# training gate: once the training is read+acknowledged, the command is enabled.

## Finished State

### Type Sub-stereotypes (b00t.type content tags)

# `pattern__learn`, `idiom__learn`, `jargon__learn` are postel sub-stereotypes of
# the `learn` topic datum type. They add:

# ```toml
# [b00t]
# type = "pattern__learn"   # inherits learn semantics; adds blessing gate

# [[b00t.blessings]]
# command = "fdfind"
# requires_ack = ["syntax", "failure_modes", "examples"]  # training sections
# enabled = false           # toggled by session state after ack
# ```

### Session State Gate (Bouncer integration)

# When agent attempts to invoke a blessed command:
# 1. Bouncer input gate checks `b00t session blessing --cmd=<command>`
# 2. If `enabled = false` → `Break("b00t learn fdfind -- not yet blessed")`
# 3. If `enabled = true` → `Continue(<command>)`
# 4. After `b00t learn <topic>` loads all required sections → auto-enable blessing

### Justfile Embedding

# Pattern datums MAY embed justfile recipes activated on blessing:

# ```toml
# [[b00t.blessings]]
# command = "fdfind"
# justfile_recipe = """
# fdfind:
#     fdfind {{pattern}} {{path}}
# """
# ```

# `b00t task bless --cmd=fdfind` → installs recipe into active justfile scope.

### Postel Normalization

# | Input `b00t.type` | Canonical form | Inherited from |
# |---|---|---|
# | `pattern__learn` | pattern__learn | learn |
# | `pattern` | pattern__learn | learn |
# | `idiom__learn` | idiom__learn | learn |
# | `idiom` | idiom__learn | learn |
# | `jargon` | jargon__learn | learn |

# `b00t datum filter --types=pattern` matches all three via `type_tags` substring.

### Naming Convention (Agent Types)

# The `__` separator encodes multiple-inheritance:
# - `agent__cli` = Agent with Cli implementations
# - `pattern__learn` = Pattern that IS a Learn topic
# - `agent__cli__sdk` = Agent implementing Cli and SDK interfaces

# This is the POSTEL extension of the existing `b00t.type` string:
# accept any `{base}__{mixin}` form; the base type's contract must be satisfied.

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `b00t.type = "pattern__learn"` datums appear in `b00t datum filter --types=pattern`
# - [ ] `b00t datum filter --types=pattern,idiom` returns pattern__learn and idiom__learn datums
# - [ ] Bouncer gate checks `b00t session blessing --cmd=<command>` before execution
# - [ ] `b00t learn <topic>` with all sections read → auto-triggers blessing for embedded cmds
# - [ ] `b00t task bless --cmd=<command>` manually enables a blessed command
# - [ ] Justfile recipe installed when blessing is granted

